-- X17 (fix-round F1, CROSS-MODULE) x14 with the colliding `display` interface
-- and its impl moved into an IMPORTED module. The entry module declares
-- nothing; its only view of the name is the `import ifcx.{Ifc, display}`
-- clause. This is the axis a single-file row cannot see: the entry-module
-- method table's own-declaration rung and its imported rungs are DIFFERENT
-- rungs (`ownMethodIdent` vs `methodCandImported`, compiler/types/typecheck.mdk),
-- so a fix that only stops an OWN declaration from capturing the wrap would
-- pass x14 and still ship the S0 here.
--
-- MEASURED ON THE SPRINT HEAD a17281e6 (cold-built in this worktree,
-- MEDAKA_STRICT=1): build ACCEPTs and the BUILT BINARY prints `HIJACKED`,
-- exactly as the single-file x14 does.
--
-- FIXED shape: the wrap resolves no name in the entry module's scope on either
-- axis (`autoPrintPinCore`, compiler/driver/main_autoprint.mdk) -- the built
-- binary must print 7. `run` REJECTs BY DESIGN (#1681: a non-Unit VALUE main)
-- -- graded BUILD_EXACT. Value hand-derived from the literal `main = 7`.
import ifcx.{Ifc, display}

main = 7
